    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p>You need a Biotech Tool Kit to modify <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Yuuzhan_Vong_Biotech\" title=\"Yuuzhan Vong Biotech\">Yuuzhan Vong Biotech</a>, install a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Bio-Implant\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Bio-Implant\">Bio-Implant</a>, or otherwise alter biological devices and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Living_Vehicles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Living Vehicles\">Living Vehicles</a>. A standard Biotech Tool Kit consists of a variety of implements and tools that look more at home in a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Medical_Kit\" title=\"Medical Kit\">Medical Kit</a> than in a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Tool_Kit\" title=\"Tool Kit\">Tool Kit</a>, and unlike a normal <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Tool_Kit\" title=\"Tool Kit\">Tool Kit</a>, items in a Biotech Tool Kit cannot be doubled as <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Improvised_Weapons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Improvised Weapons\">Improvised Weapons</a>. </p>",
